1
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:09,660
Keep running along, watch as we pass by,
as we raise our flag, up high in the sky.

2
00:00:15,800 --> 00:00:16,630
Alright,

3
00:00:16,713 --> 00:00:21,111
here we go now, sailing through the
endless ocean, facing all that comes by.

4
00:00:21,640 --> 00:00:26,937
Let's look for our treasure, nobody has
ever got to witness with their own eyes.

5
00:00:27,020 --> 00:00:31,237
All we have to do is keep
believing in our dreams.

6
00:00:31,320 --> 00:00:32,697
And let our heart lead the way.

7
00:00:32,780 --> 00:00:36,940
Then once we got all that,
all there's left is to go.

8
00:00:39,020 --> 00:00:42,297
When we face the dark and stormy weather?

9
00:00:42,380 --> 00:00:45,277
Keep the pace, we'll
link our hearts together.

10
00:00:45,360 --> 00:00:48,800
Then I'm sure we'll make it through.

11
00:00:49,480 --> 00:00:51,057
No matter what!

12
00:00:51,140 --> 00:00:54,537
Keep running along, keep running along.

13
00:00:54,620 --> 00:00:57,477
Still raising our flag as we journey on.

14
00:00:57,560 --> 00:00:59,837
Though our chances are close to none.

15
00:00:59,920 --> 00:01:02,617
We won't back down from anyone.

16
00:01:02,700 --> 00:01:06,537
Let's start up the chase,
let's start up the chase.

17
00:01:06,620 --> 00:01:09,477
Toward our own dreams
while keeping the pace.

18
00:01:09,560 --> 00:01:11,837
With a compass pointing to our goal.

19
00:01:11,920 --> 00:01:16,520
We won't stop till we've
gone around the world.

20
00:01:17,380 --> 00:01:19,020
Start me up.

21
00:01:21,320 --> 00:01:24,497
Keep running along, keep running along.

22
00:01:24,580 --> 00:01:27,457
And we'll never stop,
till we're at the top.

23
00:01:27,540 --> 00:01:29,817
There's no way that we'll ever quit.

24
00:01:29,900 --> 00:01:32,560
We'll keep heading for tomorrow.

25
00:01:33,420 --> 00:01:36,557
Let's start up the chase,
let's start up the chase.

26
00:01:36,640 --> 00:01:39,497
I see through your eyes,
what we'll have to face.

27
00:01:39,580 --> 00:01:42,097
All the memories will stay in our hearts.

28
00:01:42,180 --> 00:01:46,497
We'll never let them go, brand new world.

29
00:01:46,580 --> 00:01:48,980
Let's start me up!

30
00:02:16,680 --> 00:02:17,510
Huh?

31
00:02:19,440 --> 00:02:20,270
What?

32
00:02:20,353 --> 00:02:22,857
You're telling me we're on
the hunt for two keys now?

33
00:02:22,940 --> 00:02:24,940
One for Robin and those two bozos?

34
00:02:26,240 --> 00:02:27,120
Yeah, exactly.

35
00:02:27,540 --> 00:02:28,917
How stupid can this get?

36
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:32,176
All right, at least I know
how deep of a hole we're in

37
00:02:40,800 --> 00:02:42,741
You've really got me fired up now

38
00:02:46,580 --> 00:02:47,410
Oh, boy.

39
00:02:47,493 --> 00:02:49,860
He just won't stay down. Talk about tough.

40
00:02:50,420 --> 00:02:51,832
Oh, I'll show you tough.

41
00:02:53,620 --> 00:02:54,450
Franky!

42
00:02:59,320 --> 00:03:00,320
Destroyer cannon!

43
00:03:06,800 --> 00:03:08,660
Maybe you shouldn't do it then!

44
00:03:09,740 --> 00:03:10,570
Moron!

45
00:03:10,653 --> 00:03:11,483
That won't work.

46
00:03:11,566 --> 00:03:12,592
I'm a six powers master.

47
00:03:12,840 --> 00:03:15,134
No bullet can move as quickly as I can!

48
00:03:16,580 --> 00:03:19,417
It doesn't matter how much
you run around or how fast!

49
00:03:19,500 --> 00:03:21,937
It's practically impossible
for anyone to escape.

50
00:03:22,020 --> 00:03:23,667
my Franky Destroyer Cannon.

51
00:03:24,040 --> 00:03:28,275
These aren't just any cannons, they're
loaded with tracking cannonballs.

52
00:03:29,080 --> 00:03:30,700
Huh, tracking cannonballs?

53
00:03:30,940 --> 00:03:35,587
Does he mean they're cannonballs that
can sense their target and track it down?

54
00:03:46,580 --> 00:03:48,837
I've never even heard
of technology like that.

55
00:03:48,920 --> 00:03:50,240
This guy's amazing.

56
00:03:54,700 --> 00:03:55,530
Huh?

57
00:03:57,520 --> 00:03:58,400
Hey, wait!

58
00:03:58,740 --> 00:04:01,152
You mean all the tracking is done by you?

59
00:04:01,340 --> 00:04:03,660
How can you still run that damn fast?

60
00:04:06,860 --> 00:04:10,036
Why am I letting this idiot
chase me around like this?

61
00:04:15,700 --> 00:04:17,820
Oh, man, he disappeared again.

62
00:04:21,200 --> 00:04:22,200
Come out!

63
00:04:24,900 --> 00:04:26,680
Searching for me is pointless.

64
00:04:27,120 --> 00:04:29,238
I'm a master of the shave technique.

65
00:04:29,560 --> 00:04:33,217
With its power, not only am I
faster than the speed of lightning,

66
00:04:33,300 --> 00:04:34,980
I'm also completely silent.

67
00:04:35,180 --> 00:04:38,240
Just like an owl,
patiently hunting its prey.

68
00:04:39,520 --> 00:04:42,160
I ALWAYS carry out a
flawless assassination!

69
00:04:47,680 --> 00:04:49,220
Just like an owl, huh?

70
00:04:49,800 --> 00:04:50,630
Precisely!

71
00:04:50,713 --> 00:04:54,815
My target doesn't realize I'm upon
them until the moment of their death!

72
00:04:58,100 --> 00:04:59,800
He was hiding over here!

73
00:05:01,780 --> 00:05:04,640
Yeah, all that bragging
was real stealthy of ya.

74
00:05:05,620 --> 00:05:06,880
Cocky jerk!

75
00:05:07,240 --> 00:05:09,640
How dare you humiliate me like this!

76
00:05:10,040 --> 00:05:12,620
No one humiliates CP9 and labs!

77
00:05:13,860 --> 00:05:14,690
Shit!

78
00:05:20,960 --> 00:05:22,240
Iron Ball!

79
00:05:26,900 --> 00:05:28,520
Whoa, be careful!

80
00:05:30,160 --> 00:05:32,480
Damn it, we're over the ocean!

81
00:05:44,420 --> 00:05:45,960
This is bad.

82
00:05:47,280 --> 00:05:48,900
The current's too strong.

83
00:05:49,960 --> 00:05:52,372
It'll drag him straight to the waterfall.

84
00:05:52,960 --> 00:05:55,784
There's nothing I can do
to help him in the sea.

85
00:05:56,780 --> 00:05:57,610
Franky!

86
00:05:58,020 --> 00:05:59,640
Swim with all your might!

87
00:06:02,840 --> 00:06:03,880
Cha-ba-ba.

88
00:06:04,280 --> 00:06:05,986
No matter what, I'll be fine.

89
00:06:06,200 --> 00:06:08,494
I'll just use my moonwalk if I go over.

90
00:06:09,780 --> 00:06:10,610
Not good.

91
00:06:10,693 --> 00:06:11,677
I can hardly move.

92
00:06:11,760 --> 00:06:15,117
I've got a damn strong current,
and I'm gonna run out of air.

93
00:06:15,200 --> 00:06:18,000
I'm doubly screwed here. Cha-ba-ba.

94
00:06:18,180 --> 00:06:19,592
Just hurry up and drown.

95
00:06:21,500 --> 00:06:22,330
You're good!

96
00:06:23,940 --> 00:06:24,920
There's no way.

97
00:06:25,100 --> 00:06:26,747
He busted out of the fridge?

98
00:06:27,400 --> 00:06:28,460
Thank you!

99
00:06:28,940 --> 00:06:33,540
I am so full!

100
00:06:35,200 --> 00:06:36,660
Holy crap, he got fat!

101
00:06:37,700 --> 00:06:39,340
You cannot be serious!

102
00:06:39,660 --> 00:06:42,072
Did you eat every piece of food in there?

103
00:06:51,420 --> 00:06:54,180
I really don't have any
desire to die today!

104
00:06:56,580 --> 00:06:58,300
I'm already at the base end!

105
00:06:59,000 --> 00:06:59,830
Don't fall!

106
00:06:59,913 --> 00:07:01,360
Don't fall! Don't go over!

107
00:07:03,360 --> 00:07:05,080
Rick! Butterfly!

108
00:07:09,160 --> 00:07:10,440
Cha-pa-pa-pa!

109
00:07:10,640 --> 00:07:13,580
You are going over that
waterfall! No more!

110
00:07:22,200 --> 00:07:23,300
Solid pace!

111
00:07:28,620 --> 00:07:30,140
Ugly bastard!

112
00:07:38,320 --> 00:07:39,640
Weapons left!

113
00:07:39,880 --> 00:07:42,200
Eat this! Ha! Paper art!

114
00:07:48,440 --> 00:07:49,960
Come on!

115
00:07:50,180 --> 00:07:51,533
What the hell was that?

116
00:07:53,200 --> 00:07:54,520
So close!

117
00:07:54,980 --> 00:07:55,960
Too bad!

118
00:07:56,580 --> 00:07:57,410
Damn it!

119
00:07:57,580 --> 00:07:58,521
This is serious!

120
00:07:58,900 --> 00:08:00,782
I've got to get to shore pronto!

121
00:08:01,360 --> 00:08:03,000
One liter cola cannon!

122
00:08:04,200 --> 00:08:05,030
Udaboo!

123
00:08:09,280 --> 00:08:10,110
Joppa!

124
00:08:10,193 --> 00:08:11,857
Didn't learn your lesson, huh?

125
00:08:11,940 --> 00:08:15,352
It takes more than strength
to defeat a six powers master!

126
00:08:15,700 --> 00:08:17,700
Strong hammer! Keep her off!

127
00:08:21,500 --> 00:08:23,300
Now fall over the edge!

128
00:08:25,460 --> 00:08:27,060
Strong right!

129
00:08:32,740 --> 00:08:34,200
Let's go!

130
00:08:48,020 --> 00:08:51,217
Let me go, you jerk!

131
00:08:51,300 --> 00:08:55,359
I can't do the moonwalk with one
foot when I'm carrying someone else!

132
00:08:56,640 --> 00:08:58,260
You're gonna make us fall!

133
00:08:58,860 --> 00:09:00,380
Yeah, I realize that.

134
00:09:00,880 --> 00:09:03,177
Tell you what, I'll let go of your lane.

135
00:09:03,260 --> 00:09:05,378
After you've taken me back to shore.

136
00:09:05,820 --> 00:09:07,600
We can fight it out on land.

137
00:09:07,960 --> 00:09:10,277
Or you can put all your
energy into fighting

138
00:09:10,360 --> 00:09:12,713
me right now and see where that gets us.

139
00:09:13,260 --> 00:09:14,960
I prefer the first option.

140
00:09:15,200 --> 00:09:18,318
But if I'm going down those
falls, you're coming too.

141
00:09:18,800 --> 00:09:23,760
You and me, we're in the same boat here,
so why don't we just go back to shore?

142
00:09:26,900 --> 00:09:29,640
Good job, that's some fine kicking.

143
00:09:30,120 --> 00:09:31,100
Good, good.

144
00:09:31,520 --> 00:09:33,740
Almost there. Keep at it.

145
00:09:34,200 --> 00:09:39,220
Chubba-ba, just so you know, this battle
is gonna end as soon as we're there.

146
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:41,620
Oh, is that a fact?

147
00:09:45,100 --> 00:09:47,737
Cause I just remembered a
little technique of mine.

148
00:09:47,820 --> 00:09:50,585
That's sure to finish
you off in a single blow!

149
00:09:51,280 --> 00:09:52,380
How funny?

150
00:09:52,940 --> 00:09:55,060
That makes two of us, Fukuro.

151
00:09:58,800 --> 00:10:00,800
So, what's your plan now?

152
00:10:01,240 --> 00:10:03,017
Just take me to shore already.

153
00:10:03,100 --> 00:10:05,897
I wanna hurry up and knock you
out and get this over with?

154
00:10:05,980 --> 00:10:07,180
That's it!

155
00:10:07,520 --> 00:10:09,900
I'm sick of your talking Sick of it!

156
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:12,412
I'm gonna shut you up right here and now!

157
00:10:15,720 --> 00:10:17,840
Super cartwheel, fire and fall!

158
00:10:18,140 --> 00:10:21,728
I'm going to slam you into the
tower and smash you to pieces!

159
00:10:23,720 --> 00:10:24,720
That's your plan?

160
00:10:24,960 --> 00:10:27,960
Well, that would pulverize
me, gotta give you that!

161
00:10:28,880 --> 00:10:29,920
Franky, center!

162
00:10:35,060 --> 00:10:36,700
I've got both your legs.

163
00:10:36,920 --> 00:10:40,037
As long as I've got you bound
like this, you can't move around.

164
00:10:40,120 --> 00:10:41,377
That doesn't mean anything!

165
00:10:41,460 --> 00:10:45,717
At the speed we're going, there's
nothing you can do to slow us down now.

166
00:10:45,800 --> 00:10:47,620
Let's just see about that.

167
00:10:49,580 --> 00:10:52,140
70-millimeter caliber cola cannon.

168
00:10:52,680 --> 00:10:54,760
Just a little coot-a-bomb.

169
00:10:56,360 --> 00:10:58,120
He thugs our momentum.

170
00:10:58,940 --> 00:11:02,140
We're not even rotating anymore. Damn you!

171
00:11:02,860 --> 00:11:04,120
That's far enough.

172
00:11:04,560 --> 00:11:06,207
We're right above the shore.

173
00:11:06,820 --> 00:11:08,037
Now take this.

174
00:11:08,120 --> 00:11:12,260
70-millimeter caliber,
1.5 bats, Call power!

175
00:11:12,980 --> 00:11:14,380
Kaido! Stop it!

176
00:11:14,540 --> 00:11:16,069
What are you trying to do?

177
00:11:20,300 --> 00:11:22,940
Just give up already, you bastard!

178
00:11:24,540 --> 00:11:26,360
Kaido! Bum!

179
00:11:34,980 --> 00:11:35,810
Super!

180
00:11:46,120 --> 00:11:48,380
Where the hell is that number two key?

181
00:11:48,640 --> 00:11:49,940
Sorrel, I'm finished!

182
00:11:50,220 --> 00:11:51,240
I'm too tired!

183
00:11:51,520 --> 00:11:53,240
Give me a piggyback! No way!

184
00:11:54,960 --> 00:11:55,790
Tempest kick!

185
00:12:03,560 --> 00:12:04,390
Finger pistol!

186
00:12:04,860 --> 00:12:05,920
What was that for?

187
00:12:06,300 --> 00:12:07,797
Don't play innocent with me!

188
00:12:07,880 --> 00:12:10,037
You were just pretending
to fire that kick at them.

189
00:12:10,120 --> 00:12:11,337
You were aiming for me, weren't you?

190
00:12:11,420 --> 00:12:13,977
That's the most paranoid
accusation I've ever heard.

191
00:12:14,060 --> 00:12:16,457
But I will admit, you have
been getting in my way.

192
00:12:16,540 --> 00:12:18,037
So if you want to fight, I'm ready.

193
00:12:18,120 --> 00:12:19,002
What'd you say?

194
00:12:19,100 --> 00:12:21,817
You've been getting in my
way, you stupid herbivore!

195
00:12:21,900 --> 00:12:22,977
What are you talking about?

196
00:12:23,060 --> 00:12:25,472
I like meat just as much as the next guy.

197
00:12:25,700 --> 00:12:26,530
Wow!

198
00:12:26,613 --> 00:12:28,440
I've always wondered about this.

199
00:12:28,600 --> 00:12:29,500
You too, Zoro.

200
00:12:29,880 --> 00:12:33,857
Didn't you just ask me the other day who
you think is stronger, a giraffe or a wolf?

201
00:12:33,940 --> 00:12:36,477
The fact is that wolves
aren't much more than cunning.

202
00:12:36,560 --> 00:12:39,877
But beyond that, they aren't exactly
the most capable of creatures.

203
00:12:39,960 --> 00:12:40,790
You bastard.

204
00:12:40,960 --> 00:12:42,077
That's the final straw.

205
00:12:42,160 --> 00:12:43,977
So you want to do this right now?

206
00:12:44,060 --> 00:12:45,440
Excellent. Let's go.

207
00:12:45,720 --> 00:12:48,777
That kind of distraction won't last
long enough for us to get away.

208
00:12:48,860 --> 00:12:49,690
What?

209
00:12:49,773 --> 00:12:52,753
Well, I sure hope you have
some sort of backup plan then.

210
00:12:53,460 --> 00:12:54,754
Rock, paper, scissors.

211
00:12:54,940 --> 00:12:55,940
Whoever loses.

212
00:12:56,600 --> 00:12:58,420
has to chop off his own hand.

213
00:13:00,320 --> 00:13:03,680
That is the most terrifying
idea I've ever heard!

214
00:13:03,980 --> 00:13:06,077
I'm not done explaining, just listen.

215
00:13:06,160 --> 00:13:08,277
The first thing we do
once we get these cuffs

216
00:13:08,360 --> 00:13:11,017
off us is run like hell
until we find Chopper.

217
00:13:11,100 --> 00:13:12,417
With his medical expertise,

218
00:13:12,500 --> 00:13:15,637
he'll be able to sew the hand back
on in no time at all, understand?

219
00:13:15,720 --> 00:13:16,860
We're not ragdolls!

220
00:13:16,960 --> 00:13:18,136
Don't be ridiculous!

221
00:13:20,600 --> 00:13:21,430
Wait.

222
00:13:22,600 --> 00:13:25,077
I've got another plan to
get us out of this mess.

223
00:13:25,160 --> 00:13:27,400
I don't even want to hear it!

224
00:13:29,340 --> 00:13:32,037
We won't be able to settle
this with words alone.

225
00:13:32,120 --> 00:13:33,737
I'm ready to go when you are.

226
00:13:33,820 --> 00:13:34,917
And let's up the stakes.

227
00:13:35,000 --> 00:13:37,824
The winner gets to keep
the prey all to himself.

228
00:13:50,260 --> 00:13:51,090
What the?

229
00:14:03,860 --> 00:14:07,260
All right, Sniper King,
just hold that posture.

230
00:14:08,320 --> 00:14:09,900
You are now a sewer.

231
00:14:10,080 --> 00:14:11,492
Someone get me a lawyer!

232
00:14:11,820 --> 00:14:15,349
There is no way I am not going
to sue your ass off for this!

233
00:14:22,600 --> 00:14:23,440
Yo-yo!

234
00:14:25,920 --> 00:14:26,750
Ugh.

235
00:14:26,833 --> 00:14:30,245
I don't think I've ever seen
anyone with so little self-control.

236
00:14:30,380 --> 00:14:33,262
You gained all that weight
in just a few minutes?

237
00:14:33,880 --> 00:14:37,940
Thank you for your concern, but I'm...

238
00:14:39,440 --> 00:14:40,477
I... I...

239
00:14:40,560 --> 00:14:41,817
I...

240
00:14:41,900 --> 00:14:44,200
Who said I'm concerned about you?

241
00:14:44,380 --> 00:14:45,237
Okay, I get it.

242
00:14:45,320 --> 00:14:46,237
You're just fine.

243
00:14:46,320 --> 00:14:48,057
Don't talk with food in your mouth.

244
00:14:48,140 --> 00:14:49,820
I'm just fine.

245
00:14:50,200 --> 00:14:51,480
Yes, thank you.

246
00:14:51,640 --> 00:14:53,877
That is indeed what I was trying to...

247
00:14:53,960 --> 00:14:56,437
I don't know what you're
trying to do, but stop it!

248
00:14:56,520 --> 00:14:59,040
You're okay, I'm okay, everything's great!

249
00:14:59,260 --> 00:15:00,319
Now get back here!

250
00:15:00,460 --> 00:15:02,417
Ah, yes, yes, of course.

251
00:15:02,500 --> 00:15:03,680
Where was I again?

252
00:15:04,240 --> 00:15:06,400
I shall solve this shortly.

253
00:15:07,040 --> 00:15:08,300
Now observe.

254
00:15:09,320 --> 00:15:11,080
My life returns!

255
00:15:17,320 --> 00:15:18,150
Digest!

256
00:15:19,540 --> 00:15:20,370
Absorb!

257
00:15:21,200 --> 00:15:22,030
Complete!

258
00:15:24,840 --> 00:15:25,670
What?

259
00:15:25,753 --> 00:15:26,880
What the heck are you?

260
00:15:27,060 --> 00:15:28,500
What did you just do?

261
00:15:28,700 --> 00:15:30,935
I mean, could you do it again, please?

262
00:15:32,320 --> 00:15:33,737
A life return!

263
00:15:33,820 --> 00:15:35,137
The Digest!

264
00:15:35,220 --> 00:15:36,140
That comes off!

265
00:15:40,660 --> 00:15:41,820
So awesome!

266
00:15:42,180 --> 00:15:43,440
How do you do that?

267
00:15:43,620 --> 00:15:47,500
Well, how kind of you to ask!

268
00:15:48,040 --> 00:15:51,940
A thousand years at sea, a
thousand years in the mountains,

269
00:15:52,280 --> 00:15:55,237
breathing in the wind, than
drinking the morning dew.

270
00:15:55,320 --> 00:15:58,640
I lived as a hermit to
complete my training, and lo,

271
00:15:58,960 --> 00:16:03,260
at long last, the secrets of life
return revealed themselves to me.

272
00:16:04,980 --> 00:16:10,837
From your head down to your toes,
every inch of the human body?

273
00:16:10,920 --> 00:16:13,508
can be controlled with
the strength of will.

274
00:16:13,800 --> 00:16:19,820
Why, you can even command your internal
organs and each hair to its very tip.

275
00:16:21,100 --> 00:16:24,100
Using the mind to control
the workings of the body.

276
00:16:24,680 --> 00:16:27,517
I've read about something
similar in a medical journal.

277
00:16:27,600 --> 00:16:30,080
They called it biofeedback.

278
00:16:30,800 --> 00:16:35,506
Then you're able to move your hair around
like an octopus because of that power?

279
00:16:36,300 --> 00:16:37,920
Oh! Yo-yo!

280
00:16:38,180 --> 00:16:39,197
An octopus?

281
00:16:39,280 --> 00:16:40,720
How rude of you!

282
00:16:41,640 --> 00:16:44,700
I am, as you say,

283
00:16:45,200 --> 00:16:48,680
a CC!

284
00:16:49,820 --> 00:16:53,940
A valiant lion, in other words!

285
00:16:54,420 --> 00:16:56,620
Octopus, lion, whatever.

286
00:16:57,640 --> 00:16:59,320
Life return!

287
00:17:00,080 --> 00:17:01,540
And hair bite!

288
00:17:05,840 --> 00:17:08,080
Yo-yo-yoy!

289
00:17:14,120 --> 00:17:15,920
Oh, no!

290
00:17:17,280 --> 00:17:19,809
If I get caught by his
hair, it's all over.

291
00:17:20,660 --> 00:17:21,540
Where'd he go?

292
00:17:27,880 --> 00:17:28,840
Finger pistol!

293
00:17:33,640 --> 00:17:35,740
He did that with a blunt stick?

294
00:17:44,080 --> 00:17:45,040
Iron body!

295
00:17:53,780 --> 00:17:55,120
What is the matter?

296
00:17:56,420 --> 00:17:58,280
Damn it. I thought so.

297
00:17:58,660 --> 00:18:03,072
Unless I can hit him with arm point or
horn point, he's not going to budge.

298
00:18:05,020 --> 00:18:07,440
But the rumble balls are powerful.

299
00:18:08,140 --> 00:18:10,669
One in six hours is
about all I can handle.

300
00:18:11,280 --> 00:18:13,917
Any more than that will put
too much strain on my body.

301
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:15,520
Even worse,

302
00:18:15,800 --> 00:18:20,400
if I take another, I might not be able
to control my transformations anymore.

303
00:18:20,860 --> 00:18:23,617
If I still can't win and
I have to take a third,

304
00:18:23,700 --> 00:18:25,935
I might completely lose consciousness.

305
00:18:26,260 --> 00:18:27,280
Is it worth it?

306
00:18:27,740 --> 00:18:30,328
I don't think I could
damage him without it.

307
00:18:32,760 --> 00:18:36,900
I shall skewer you and roast you alive!

308
00:18:39,220 --> 00:18:40,540
Chess, come on!

309
00:18:56,460 --> 00:18:58,636
I don't have time to think this over.

310
00:18:58,940 --> 00:18:59,770
Rumble!

311
00:19:01,320 --> 00:19:05,440
It's a risk, but it's the only
chance I've got to do or die.

312
00:19:05,720 --> 00:19:08,737
One way or another, I have to
settle this in three minutes.

313
00:19:08,820 --> 00:19:09,650
Take this!

314
00:19:10,180 --> 00:19:11,010
Harpoin!

315
00:19:18,580 --> 00:19:19,410
Shishikabob!

316
00:19:21,340 --> 00:19:22,170
Take this!

317
00:19:22,253 --> 00:19:23,083
Jumping point!

318
00:19:25,380 --> 00:19:26,210
Wrong one!

319
00:19:32,560 --> 00:19:33,390
Yo-yo-yay!

320
00:19:33,900 --> 00:19:35,180
Ah, yo-yo-yay.

321
00:19:41,740 --> 00:19:42,580
Damn it.

322
00:19:42,960 --> 00:19:44,136
Just like I thought.

323
00:19:44,400 --> 00:19:46,360
My transformations are messed up.

324
00:19:46,840 --> 00:19:48,840
All I need is to get to arm point.

325
00:19:49,300 --> 00:19:51,947
One shot with a cloven
hoof should be enough.

326
00:19:52,360 --> 00:19:55,536
If this fire keeps spreading,
I'll end up suffocating.

327
00:19:55,680 --> 00:19:59,657
I can't waste time fighting this
guy when he doesn't even have a key.

328
00:19:59,740 --> 00:20:00,570
That's right.

329
00:20:00,660 --> 00:20:02,960
I have to find key number two.

330
00:20:04,180 --> 00:20:06,720
Zoro and Sniper King are counting on me.

331
00:20:07,340 --> 00:20:09,920
We can't save Robin without their help.

332
00:20:13,400 --> 00:20:15,140
Robin, hold on.

333
00:20:15,440 --> 00:20:17,280
I won't let you down.

334
00:20:19,320 --> 00:20:22,277
I'm here to save my friend.

335
00:20:22,360 --> 00:20:25,460
And I'm not going to let
anybody get in my way.

336
00:20:26,060 --> 00:20:29,060
You're a stubborn beast, aren't you?

337
00:20:30,460 --> 00:20:31,780
Life return!

338
00:20:42,880 --> 00:20:48,420
his hair is pointing at me who cares I
don't have time to think I have to win
